Following a board decision to restrict all AWS workloads to the us-east-1 and eu-west-1 regions, the cloud governance team attaches the following SCP to the root of the organization:

```json
{
  "Version": "2012-10-17",
  "Statement": [
    {
      "Effect": "Deny",
      "Action": "*",
      "Resource": "*",
      "Condition": {
        "StringNotEquals": {
          "aws:RequestedRegion": ["us-east-1", "eu-west-1"]
        }
      }
    }
  ]
}
```

After the SCP is applied, several IAM administrators report that they can no longer create IAM users, even when operating from us-east-1. What is the MOST likely cause?
